"In Bayesian hypothesis testing, P(H|E) = P(E|H)P(H) / P(E). H is a perceptual hypothesis and E is the image received. P(H) is the prior probability of percept H. P(E|H) is the probability of seeing image E if H is correct. P(E) is the probability of seeing E under any hypothesis. People start with a prior and use additional evidence to update it, as described by Kording and Wolpert (2006).",
