"Four approaches to object perception are compared. They are Helmholtz’s unconscious inference, the Gestalt laws of organization, regularities in the environment and Bayesian inference. Helmholtz, regularities and Bayesian inference all use data about the environment gathered through past experience. Top-down processing is important in all three. The classical Gestalt position emphasizes built-in principles that can override experience."
