"The measure is fixation duration, which is how long the eyes rest on a word. In “the cast worked,” both meanings of “cast” are activated. Readers look longer at “cast” than at the control word “cook.” In “the tin was,” the dominant meaning of “tin” is favored. Readers read “tin” as fast as a control word.",
