"An event-related potential (ERP) is a rapid electrical response of the brain, measured in fractions of a second after a stimulus. Two components are the N400 and the P600. A semantic violation is associated with the N400, at about 400 milliseconds. A syntactic violation is associated with the P600, at about 600 milliseconds.",
