"answers": [
"The word superiority effect means a letter is identified more accurately inside a word than alone. After a brief display, the observer chooses between two letters. Both letters would make a real word, so knowing that it was a word does not give the answer. The advantage for words remains. Top-down word knowledge supports recognition of the letter.",
"A lexical decision task asks whether a string of letters is a real word. GIRL is a word and XLFFE is not. A word is recognized faster after a related word than after an unrelated word. High frequency words are also recognized faster than low frequency words. Pseudohomophones are nonwords that sound like real words. They are harder to reject, because the pronunciation activates a familiar word."
],
