"q": "What does the Brown-Peterson procedure show?",
"a": "The Brown-Peterson procedure presents a trigram, which is a group of three letters, followed by a number. Participants count backward by threes before recalling the letters. Counting blocks maintenance rehearsal, which is repeating the material to keep it available. Recall drops steeply over about 15 to 20 seconds. Decay is forgetting with the passage of time. Recall is better on the first trial than on later trials. Proactive interference is old information disrupting new information. Retroactive interference is new information disrupting old information.",
