"q": "How did Ebbinghaus (1885/1913) measure forgetting?",
"a": "Ebbinghaus (1885/1913) measured how quickly learned information is lost over time. He used nonsense syllables, which reduce the help that familiar meanings give. He read a list aloud many times and counted the repetitions needed to repeat it without errors. After a delay, he relearned the list. Short delays meant fewer repetitions to relearn. He used many lists and many retention intervals, which are the delays between learning and relearning.",
