"q": "What is savings, and what does the savings curve show?",
"a": "Savings equals the original time to learn the list minus the time to relearn it after a delay. More savings means more benefit from the earlier learning. With 1,000 seconds of original learning, relearning after 19 minutes took 400 seconds, so 600 seconds were saved. After one day, relearning took 650 seconds, so 350 seconds were saved. After six days, relearning took 730 seconds, so 270 seconds were saved. Percent savings is the saved time divided by the original learning time, multiplied by 100. The savings curve shows savings at each retention interval. Savings drops rapidly at first and then more slowly.",
"score": 9,
