"a": "John Watson (1878–1958) saw two problems with introspection. Results were extremely variable from person to person. Results were also difficult to verify, because they were explained by invisible inner processes. Watson proposed behaviorism. Behaviorism removes the mind as a topic of study and studies directly observable behavior. Reasoning, thinking and emotions were left out because they cannot be observed.",
