"q": "What did Watson’s behaviorist manifesto (1913) set as the goal of psychology?",
"a": "Watson’s behaviorist manifesto (1913) called psychology “a purely objective experimental branch of natural science.” The goal was to predict and control behavior without appealing to consciousness. Observable stimuli and responses were the basis for explanation.",
