"q": "What happened in the Little Albert experiment of Watson and Rayner (1920), and what kind of conditioning is it?",
"a": "Watson and Rayner (1920) studied the conditioning of fear in the Little Albert experiment. A nine-month-old child became frightened by a rat after a loud noise was paired with the rat. The rat did not cause this fear at first. After the pairings, the rat alone caused fear. This is classical conditioning, because the key relationship is between two stimuli. It is not operant conditioning, which works through the consequences of an action.",
