"q": "What is classical conditioning, and how did Pavlov come to study it?",
"a": "In classical conditioning, a neutral stimulus is paired with a stimulus that naturally produces a response. After repeated pairings, the neutral stimulus produces the response. Pavlov studied digestion. Conditioning came from his observation of anticipatory salivation, which is salivation before the food arrives.",
