"q": "Why does changing the starting point test what the rat learned?",
"a": "From arm A, a right turn reaches the food in arm B. From arm C, reaching B needs a left turn. The food location stays the same and the required turn changes. A learned “turn right” response predicts a right turn. Knowing where the food is predicts a left turn.",
