"q": "What is a cognitive map, and why did Tolman conclude the rats had one?",
"a": "A simple behaviorist account says the rats learned “turn right to find food.” The rats turned left from the new starting point, so that account was not supported. Tolman believed the rats had formed a cognitive map. A cognitive map is a mental representation of the layout of the maze. Turning right had been rewarded, and the map still pointed to a left turn from arm C.",
