"q": "What dates belong to the cognitive revolution?",
"a": "The dates of the cognitive revolution include Tolman’s cognitive map in 1948, Cherry’s attention experiment in 1953 and the first commercially available digital computer in 1954. The Dartmouth and MIT conferences are dated 1956. They are followed by Skinner’s Verbal Behavior in 1957, Broadbent’s flow diagram in 1958, Chomsky’s review in 1959 and Neisser’s cognitive psychology book in 1967. The maze experiment is dated 1938, and the cognitive map is dated 1948.",
