"q": "How is perception defined, and what four properties does it have?",
"a": "Perception is experience resulting from stimulation of the senses. Every other kind of cognition starts from it. Four properties matter. Perceptions change when information is added. Perception involves a process much like reasoning or problem solving. Perceptions occur together with actions. Prior knowledge shapes how we resolve ambiguous stimuli.",
