"q": "How has machine vision changed since 2007, and what problems remain?",
"a": "In 2007, machine vision relied on hand-written rules and on combining sensors. Vehicles finished a 60-mile urban course slowly, on a closed course. Now deep networks trained on millions of labeled images match or exceed human accuracy on benchmark object recognition. Four problems remain. They are novel viewpoints, occlusion, unusual lighting, and scenes with odd context.",
