"q": "What is the inverse projection problem?",
"a": "The inverse projection problem is the task of determining which object produced a particular image on the retina. We start with the retinal image and work outward to its source. One image could have come from infinitely many objects. A small object nearby and a huge object far away can produce identical retinal images.",
