"q": "How do direct and constructive theories of perception differ?",
"a": "Direct perception theories say that perception comes from the stimuli available in the environment. Gibson emphasized the optic array, which is the pattern of light available to a moving observer. It specifies the layout of the scene. Constructive perception theories say that people actively construct perceptions using expectations. Knowledge, experience and context do part of the work. Illusions show that what is perceived can depart from the stimulus.",
