"a": "The recognition-by-components theory of Irving Biederman (1987) says we perceive objects by first perceiving elementary three-dimensional features. These building blocks are called geons. About 36 geons are proposed. Three geons in the right arrangement identify most common objects. The same parts can form different objects when they are arranged differently.",
