"q": "Why do almost all people see two overlapping rectangles?",
"a": "A retinal image, labeled (a), could come from two sources. Source (b) is two overlapping rectangles. Source (c) is a rectangle and an oddly notched shape lined up exactly. Both sources fit the image. Almost everyone chooses (b).",
