"slides": [
14
],
"q": "What happens to the attended message in Treisman’s theory?",
"a": "In Treisman’s theory, the attended message passes through the attenuator at full strength. A full strength message gives stronger input to the dictionary unit, so it is more likely to activate words.",
"score": 6,
"tier": "low",
"kind": "slide",
"id": 7312
