"q": "What happens to the unattended message in Treisman’s theory?",
"a": "The unattended message passes through at a much weaker strength. It is attenuated, and it is not shut off. A weak message can still activate a word if that word’s threshold is low enough.",
"score": 6,
"tier": "low",
