"q": "What is a late selection model, and what did MacKay (1973) present?",
"a": "In late selection models, selection for final processing does not occur until after the information has been analyzed for meaning. In MacKay (1973), the attended ear heard “They were throwing stones at the bank.” The unattended ear received either “river” or “money.”",
