"q": "What did MacKay (1973) find?",
"a": "In MacKay (1973), participants chose which test sentence was closest in meaning to the attended sentence. One test sentence was about the side of a river, and the other was about a savings and loan association. The meaning of the biasing word shifted the choice. “River” favored the river sentence, and “money” favored the financial sentence. Participants were unaware that the biasing words had been presented.",
