"q": "How do Broadbent (1958), Treisman (1964) and late selection compare?",
"a": "Broadbent (1958) proposed the filter model. Selection is early, before meaning is analyzed. Only the attended channel gets through, selected by physical features. Treisman (1964) proposed attenuation theory. Selection is intermediate. Unattended input is weakened, and low threshold words can still be activated. Deutsch and Deutsch (1963) and MacKay (1973) support late selection. Information is analyzed for meaning before selection controls response and awareness.",
