"q": "What do processing capacity and perceptual load mean in load theory?",
"a": "Processing capacity is how much information a person can handle at any given moment. Perceptual load is the difficulty of a given task. High load tasks use more processing capacity. Low load tasks use less. When a task leaves spare capacity, task-irrelevant stimuli are processed and can interfere.",
