"q": "What are overt and covert attention, saccades and fixations?",
"a": "Overt attention shifts by moving the eyes. Covert attention shifts while the eyes stay fixed. Saccades are rapid eye movements from one place to another. Fixations are short pauses on points of interest. An eye tracker measures both. Central vision is the area being looked at, and it falls on the fovea. Peripheral vision is off to the side. The fovea has much higher resolution than the periphery.",
