"q": "What is stimulus salience?",
"a": "Stimulus salience refers to areas that stand out and capture attention. It is a bottom-up process that depends on the physical characteristics of the stimulus. Color and motion are highly salient. Attentional capture is an involuntary shift of attention due to stimulus salience.",
