"q": "What is the same-object advantage, and how did Egly and colleagues (1994) test it?",
"a": "The same-object advantage shows that we can covertly attend to specific objects. When attention is directed to one place on an object, its effect spreads to other places on that object. In Egly and colleagues (1994), a cue was followed by a target at the cued position, at another position on the same object, or on a different object. The two uncued positions were the same distance from the cue.",
