"q": "What is naturalistic driving research, and why is it quasi-experimental?",
"a": "Cognitive psychology “in the wild” studies behavior with no experimenter present. The naturalistic driving work collected data in privately owned vehicles with unobtrusive instruments. These included hidden radar, a face camera behind smoked glass, and other cameras about one inch by one inch. The design is quasi-experimental. Researchers observe crashes that happen naturally and examine what was happening before each crash.",
