"q": "What did the 100-car database hold, and how were crashes, near crashes and incidents defined?",
"a": "The 100-car database held 42,300 hours of driving, about two million miles. It had 82 crashes and collisions, 761 near crashes, 8,295 incidents and 20,000 matched periods of normal baseline driving. A crash or collision is contact with another vehicle, a fixed object, a pedestrian, a pedalcyclist or an animal. A near crash is a conflict that requires a rapid, severe evasive maneuver. An incident requires a smaller evasive maneuver.",
