"q": "How much did inattention contribute to crashes in the 100-car study?",
"a": "In the 100-car results, inattention to the forward roadway was a primary contributing factor in many crashes. 80 percent of crashes and 65 percent of near crashes involved at least one form of inattention within three seconds before the conflict began. 93 percent of lead-vehicle crashes and minor collisions involved looking away. In 86 percent of those, the headway was greater than 2.0 seconds. Headway is the time gap between vehicles.",
