"q": "What do the birdhouse passage, the nail sentence and the N400 study show about reading?",
"a": "Readers infer things that the text never says, such as the hammer. They simulate what is described, so a horizontal nail is identified faster. They use event knowledge, so “guitar” gave a smaller N400 than “barn” at a concert.",
"score": 8.5,
"tier": "high",
